# Advanced Phaser Audio Techniques

## Context
- When implementing dynamic or adaptive audio systems
- When creating immersive audio experiences
- When implementing spatial audio or positional sound effects
- When creating games requiring complex audio layering, mixing, or transitions

## Requirements
- Use Phaser's WebAudio capabilities for advanced audio processing
- Implement dynamic music systems that adapt to gameplay
- Create smooth transitions between different audio states
- Apply audio effects and filters for enhanced immersion
- Implement categories for selective audio management

## Examples

```typescript
// Advanced audio techniques implementation
export class AdvancedAudioManager {
  private scene: Phaser.Scene;
  private music: Map<string, Phaser.Sound.BaseSound> = new Map();
  private currentMusic: string | null = null;
  private transitionTime: number = 1000; // ms
  
  // Audio categories for selective control
  private categories: Map<string, Set<Phaser.Sound.BaseSound>> = new Map([
    ['sfx', new Set()],
    ['music', new Set()],
    ['voice', new Set()],
    ['ui', new Set()],
    ['ambient', new Set()]
  ]);
  
  // Audio effects
  private filters: Map<string, any> = new Map();
  
  constructor(scene: Phaser.Scene) {
    this.scene = scene;
    
    // Set up WebAudio effects
    this.setupAudioEffects();
  }
  
  /**
   * Set up WebAudio effects for processing
   */
  private setupAudioEffects(): void {
    if (this.scene.sound.context) {
      // Create a low-pass filter
      const lowpassFilter = this.scene.sound.context.createBiquadFilter();
      lowpassFilter.type = 'lowpass';
      lowpassFilter.frequency.value = 1000;
      this.filters.set('lowpass', lowpassFilter);
      
      // Create a reverb effect
      this.createReverb(2, 0.5).then(reverb => {
        this.filters.set('reverb', reverb);
      });
    }
  }
  
  /**
   * Create a reverb effect
   */
  private async createReverb(seconds: number, decay: number): Promise<any> {
    const context = this.scene.sound.context;
    if (!context) return null;
    
    const length = seconds * context.sampleRate;
    const impulse = context.createBuffer(2, length, context.sampleRate);
    
    const left = impulse.getChannelData(0);
    const right = impulse.getChannelData(1);
    
    for (let i = 0; i < length; i++) {
      const n = i / length;
      // Simple exponential decay
      left[i] = (Math.random() * 2 - 1) * Math.pow(1 - n, decay);
      right[i] = (Math.random() * 2 - 1) * Math.pow(1 - n, decay);
    }
    
    const reverb = context.createConvolver();
    reverb.buffer = impulse;
    
    return reverb;
  }
  
  /**
   * Cross-fade between two music tracks
   */
  crossFadeMusic(newMusicKey: string, duration: number = 1000): void {
    const newMusic = this.music.get(newMusicKey);
    if (!newMusic) return;
    
    // If no current music, just play the new track
    if (!this.currentMusic) {
      newMusic.play();
      this.currentMusic = newMusicKey;
      return;
    }
    
    const currentMusic = this.music.get(this.currentMusic);
    if (!currentMusic) return;
    
    // Start new music at zero volume
    newMusic.setVolume(0);
    newMusic.play();
    
    // Fade out current music and fade in new music
    const startTime = this.scene.time.now;
    const endTime = startTime + duration;
    
    // Set up a tween for smooth transition
    this.scene.tweens.add({
      targets: { t: 0 },
      t: 1,
      duration: duration,
      onUpdate: (tween) => {
        const t = tween.getValue();
        currentMusic.setVolume(1 - t);
        newMusic.setVolume(t);
      },
      onComplete: () => {
        currentMusic.stop();
        this.currentMusic = newMusicKey;
      }
    });
  }
  
  /**
   * Apply audio effect to a sound
   */
  applyEffect(sound: Phaser.Sound.WebAudioSound, effectKey: string, amount: number = 1.0): void {
    if (!sound || !(sound instanceof Phaser.Sound.WebAudioSound)) return;
    
    const effect = this.filters.get(effectKey);
    if (!effect) return;
    
    // Get source node from WebAudio sound
    const source = sound.source;
    if (!source) return;
    
    // Connect the source to the effect, then to destination
    source.disconnect();
    source.connect(effect);
    effect.connect(this.scene.sound.context.destination);
  }
  
  /**
   * Create an adaptive music system based on game state
   */
  updateAdaptiveMusic(intensity: number): void {
    // Adjust music parameters based on gameplay intensity
    const currentMusic = this.music.get(this.currentMusic || '');
    if (!currentMusic) return;
    
    // Modify rate slightly for increased tension
    const newRate = 1.0 + (intensity * 0.2); // Max 20% faster
    currentMusic.setRate(newRate);
    
    // Apply low-pass filter during high intensity
    if (currentMusic instanceof Phaser.Sound.WebAudioSound && this.filters.has('lowpass')) {
      const lowpass = this.filters.get('lowpass');
      
      // More filtering at high intensity
      const filterFreq = 20000 - (intensity * 15000); // Range: 5000 - 20000 Hz
      lowpass.frequency.value = filterFreq;
    }
  }
}
```

## Dynamic Audio
- Adapt music and sound effects based on gameplay conditions
- Transition between different game states with audio cues
- Layer multiple audio tracks for dynamic mix
- Change audio parameters based on player actions
- Design music systems that respond to game events

## Spatial Audio
- Position sounds in the game world
- Attenuate volume based on distance from listener
- Apply filters based on environment (e.g., reverb in caves)
- Pan sounds based on relative position to camera
- Simulate doppler effect for moving sound sources

## Audio Categories
- Group sounds into logical categories
- Control volume independently for each category
- Apply effects to entire categories
- Mute or unmute categories based on game state
- Prioritize sounds based on category importance

